            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Dimorphotheca fruticosa, is a species of perennial herb native to coastal areas of South Africa. It is commonly known as trailing African daisy, and by its synonym Osteospermum fruticosum."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "It has been classified as a weed in New Zealand where it is now a widespread coastal plant, particularly in the North Island."
          }
        ]
      }
